---
description: Spring Boot conventions and spec-driven workflow
alwaysApply: true
---
- Do not implement any feature without an active OpenSpec change; follow its tasks.md in order.
- Base package is com.example.task_manager. Java 17, Maven.
- Layers: Controller -> Service -> Repository. No business logic in controllers.
- Use DTOs (records) for request/response; never expose JPA entities directly.
- Validate input with Bean Validation (@Valid, @NotBlank, etc.).
- Handle errors in one @RestControllerAdvice returning a consistent error body.
- Tests: JUnit 5; @WebMvcTest for controllers, @DataJpaTest for repositories, Mockito for service unit tests.
- Every task must have at least one test before it is checked off in tasks.md.
- Commit format: feat(<change-name>): <task-id> <summary>
- If the implementation contradicts the spec, stop and update the spec and tasks first.
